  <h3>Conclusion</h3><p>India’s overtaking of Japan is both a symbolic and substantive milestone in the 21st-century economic race. While challenges remain — unemployment, inequality, and climate stress — the trajectory suggests that India is poised not only to sustain its growth but also to reshape global governance. Its success will hinge on balancing growth with equity, and ambition with sustainability.</p>
